romptState":{"text":"subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1>: The adult woman shown in <Picture 1>, used only as the replacement-person appearance reference: medium-deep brown skin, the same facial identity and proportions, dark eyebrows, brown eyes, full lips, and long dense black naturally curly hair. Preserve her recognizable identity base from <Picture 1>, but in the edited result her face and hair must appear heavily soaked, with water as a dominant visible layer over her skin and features. Do not transfer the reference image's background, framing, visible text, fruit, or composition; only transfer her identity, hair type, complexion, and overall appearance.\n<Video 1>: The supplied source MP4 is the direct video-editing source. Preserve its complete temporal structure, framing, camera movement, shot order, setting, lighting, props, actions, and editing pattern, while replacing only the original visible woman with <Subject 1> and strongly emphasizing a drenched, shower-wet appearance.\n<Audio 1>: The original synchronized audio track embedded in <Video 1>, copied unchanged and kept locked to the original video timing.\n\nsummary:\n[video editing + audio reuse] Replace the original visible woman throughout <Video 1> with <Subject 1>, preserving the source video and synchronized <Audio 1> while making the soaked, water-covered appearance of <Subject 1> extremely prominent, with her face visibly drenched and partially obscured by water.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1> (appears throughout the edited source wherever the original woman appears): fully_preserved - preserve the reference woman's facial identity, complexion, wet curly hair type, and overall appearance, while making heavy water coverage across her face, hair, and skin a defining visible characteristic.\n<Video 1> (provides the entire edited sequence): partially_preserved - preserve all source timing, framing, camera behavior, environment, lighting, props, interactions, and edit structure while replacing the original woman's visible appearance.\n<Audio 1> (runs throughout the edited sequence): fully_copy - retain the original synchronized source audio signal unchanged, without re-timing or regeneration.\n\ndetailed_description:\nPhotorealistic vertical social-media video with the same phone-camera realism, exposure behavior, texture, and natural imperfections as <Video 1>. The result must read as a seamless identity replacement, with an unusually strong emphasis on visible water, moisture, and soaking over <Subject 1>'s face and hair.\n[Shot 1] Use <Video 1> as the exact full-length motion and composition source. Wherever the original woman appears, replace her continuously with <Subject 1>, keeping her head, neck, shoulders, torso, arms, and hands locked to the source performance on every frame. Preserve <Subject 1>'s identity from <Picture 1>, but make the drenched look unmistakable and visually dominant: her forehead, temples, eyebrows, eyelashes, cheeks, nose, lips, chin, jawline, neck, collarbones, shoulders, and visible upper chest must be covered with clear beads, droplets, rivulets, and thin streaming sheets of water. The water must not look subtle or incidental; it must be obvious at first glance and remain obvious throughout the shot. Her facial features should still belong to <Subject 1>, but the heavy wetness should make them harder to read, with water clinging over the skin, crossing the face in uneven paths, collecting along the lashes and lips, and catching highlights so strongly that her face feels almost unrecognizable under the soaking layer. Her curls must look thoroughly saturated, darker from the water, clumped into wet ringlets, and stuck in places to her forehead, temples, cheeks, and neck, with individual strands hanging heavy and dripping. Preserve every original expression, blink, gaze change, head motion, body motion, hand movement, and prop interaction from <Video 1>, but integrate the water into those actions so droplets shift, slide, and break apart naturally with each movement. If the source includes close facial framing, make the water even more visually assertive, with continuous reflective sheen, fresh droplets forming, and runoff descending from the hairline over the face. If a hand touches the face or passes near it, preserve the contact while showing wet skin, glossy reflections, and convincing moisture transfer. Maintain accurate occlusion, perspective, and motion blur so the replacement remains fully integrated. Match the source lighting, but ensure the water produces visible specular highlights and a glossy drenched sheen across the face and skin. Preserve exact mouth and jaw movement from the source wherever vocal audio exists, while keeping the wet lips, wet skin, and damp facial texture stable and believable. All source background elements, timing, and edit decisions remain unchanged unless reconstruction is required to support the replacement and the intensified water coverage.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nKeep <Audio 1> synchronized exactly to <Video 1>. Retain its continuous ambient floor and all physical source sounds at their original timing and level, without adding, duplicating, removing, or re-timing audible events.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nPreserve any audience-only music already contained in <Audio 1> exactly at its original timing, instrumentation, rhythm, dynamics, and level; add no new music.","order":"mine","sep":", ","accent":null,"showExpanded":false}},"widgets_values":[""],"color":"#14436c","bgcolor":"#2a2a2a"},{"id":223,"type":"PixaromaSizes","pos":[-509.51259285471383,217.83035566381673],"size":[240,534],"flags":{},"order":10,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[{"localized_name":"width","name":"width","type":"INT","links":[281]},{"localized_name":"height","name":"height","type":"INT","links":[282]}],"title":"1. Pick Orientation and Size","properties":{"aux_id":"ComfyUI-Pixaroma.git","ver":"a13e16f26ce1b1de096fe97ded9b95ec3d2b62ab","Node name for S&R":"PixaromaSizes","cnr_id":"C